# OPTIONAL headless fallback. Self-signed/internal-CA certificates for
# connectors are normally trusted in the WebUI (connector Configure dialog ->
# Fetch Certificate -> Trust this certificate), which stores the pin with the
# connector; a pin set there takes precedence over anything in this file.
# Use this file only to pre-provision trust from the shell, e.g.
# for an unattended install.
#
# One line per trusted connector INSTANCE, keyed by its connector ID, not per connector
# type — the worker runs one thread per registered connector (see
# runner.py), so 8 Kubernetes Dashboard registrations need 8 different
# certs, each keyed by its own connector_id.
#
# Copy this file to .env.connector-certs to get started (or just run the
# script — it creates the real file for you on first use). The real file
# is gitignored; this .example file is the only one that gets committed.
#
# Example line (do not use this value — it's illustrative only):
# DASHBOARD_CA_CERT_B64__a1b2c3d4_e5f6_4789_a012_b3c4d5e6f789=LS0tLS1CRUdJTiBDRVJUSUZJQ0FURS0tLS0t...
